:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.20.19a</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<div class="dolx-changelog-label">v0.20.19a (PATCH)</div>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Buffed Shrine's Fortune and added Four-Leaf Fortune</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Shrine's Fortune</strong> now increases Luck by 40% for one day.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Four-Leaf Fortune</strong>, which increases Luck by 7% while you keep the four-leaf clover.</li>
		<li>Both bonuses can stack.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated AMC trait tooltips</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>All 28 selectable AMC traits now have hover tooltips showing the exact stat they enhance.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>

		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Chest binders now relieve chest dysphoria</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Chest dysphoria now uses apparent breast size, so binders and sports bras flatten the player's chest as expected.</li>
		<li>Properly worn binders can occasionally cause chest pain.</li>
		<li>Torn or displaced binders no longer flatten the chest or cause pressure discomfort.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>

		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed global fatigue cap initialization</strong></li>

		<li><strong>Fixed Tempered Milk and Semen Volume</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Tempered Milk</strong> and <strong>Semen Volume</strong> are mutually exclusive again.</li>
		<li>Affected saves repair automatically.</li>
		<li>Liquid capacity now updates correctly when Cow, Bull, or Alpha effects change.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>

		<li><strong>Fixed food</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The player can no longer eat mugs.</li>
		<li>Fixed the Journal breaking in some food-related cases.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>

		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney X-Change encounters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Whitney's X-Change encounter now correctly checks whether it started in the alley or at school.</li>
		<li>Removed reliance on an unused location flag that could carry the previous encounter's location into a later scene.</li>
		<li>The encounter now uses the game's existing location data instead.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>

		<li><strong>Fixed Arousal Acclimated checks</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Arousal Acclimated</strong> now works consistently anywhere high Arousal can block choices.</li>
		<li>The player can leave Wren's card game while aroused.</li>
		<li>Recently orgasming now correctly allows sleeping or leaving the bath at home, on the farm, and in Alex's cottage.</li>
		<li>The bath's <strong>Will yourself to get out</strong> option now appears when the player has enough Willpower.</li>
		<li>Updated the setting description to list all choices unlocked by the trait.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>

		<li><strong>Fixed mirror menus remembering the wrong screen</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Closing the POCKET mirror inside a submenu, such as Makeup or Hair, no longer makes the next mirror open to that same submenu.</li>
		<li>Fixed menu state carrying between other mirrors, including the park and school toilets.</li>
		<li>Mirror interactions that intentionally return to the same submenu still work as before.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>

		<li><strong>Fixed the full-body character view</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The full-body view now fits correctly when using <strong>Options &gt; Advanced &gt; Zoom</strong>.</li>
		<li>It resizes properly at any zoom level and updates immediately when the Zoom setting changes while the view is open.</li>
		<li>Closing the full-body view now stops its animation instead of leaving it running in the background.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>

		<hr>
		<div class="dolx-changelog-label">v0.20.19 (PREVIOUS RELEASE)</div>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added the POCKET menu</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Replaced the sidebar <strong>DECOMOD</strong> button with <strong>POCKET</strong>, opening on the Bag tab and also containing the Hand Mirror.</li>
		<li>The player always has one personal POCKET slot. Bags add extra slots by type: backpack 8, suitcase/luggage 10, tote/gym bag 6, messenger bag 5, purse 2.</li>
		<li>Each item type uses one slot regardless of quantity.</li>
		<li>Cooked food can be packed from the kitchen, medicine from the medicine drawer, and toys from the toy cupboard.</li>
		<li>Food and medicine can be used from most locations. Packed toys act as a portable toy cupboard and do not count toward the normal five-toy carry limit.</li>
		<li>Removing or swapping a bag empties only that bag's packed slots; owned items remain safely stored at home.</li>
		<li>POCKET is disabled during combat, dancing, capture, trance, Hopeless Cycle, flashbacks, replays, frozen scenes, and bad ends.</li>
		<li>Added a Hand Mirror sold at the cosmetics store for a base price of £15 before inflation. It opens the full mirror, including appearance, hair, makeup, DecoMod, and transformation controls, from most locations.</li>
		<li>The Hand Mirror cannot be used during a Blood Moon.</li>
		<li>Every edible cooked dish can now be eaten. Cafe food also increases fullness except where soft bad ends use separate mechanics.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Well Fed</strong>, lasting roughly 2–5 hours depending on the meal. While active, incoming Stress, Trauma, Pain, and Tiredness build 5% slower.</li>
		<li>Added fullness and <strong>Bloated</strong>. Eating above the fullness limit causes Bloated for 10 hours and adds 5% points to skill-failure checks.</li>
		<li>Added the feat <strong>Own Two Hands</strong> for eating 100 servings of your own cooking.</li>
		<li>Added an optional <strong>Food Spoilage</strong> Rebalancing setting, off by default. Cooked food is stored in dated batches, eaten oldest-first, and shown in <strong>Journal &gt; Inventory &gt; Foods</strong>.</li>
		<li>When spoilage is disabled, expired food remains edible but loses its direct stat effects while still giving fullness and Well Fed.</li>
		<li>Rebalanced market-stall values for cooked dishes so meal value better reflects how substantial the serving is.</li>
		<li>Cooking can now use breast milk as a substitute for milk.</li>
		<li>Eating your own cooking through POCKET can grant animal transformation points based on the dish. Cow is excluded because it remains Remy's specialty.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added daytime Willpower recovery</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Relaxing actions can now restore some Willpower without sleeping, including praying, meditating, resting, and eating a proper meal.</li>
		<li>Packed food in bag counts as a meal for recovery.</li>
		<li>Daytime recovery is capped at 40% of maximum Willpower per day.</li>
		<li>Autism Spectrum characters also reduce Load while resting, even when Stress does not change.</li>
		<li>Added related options under <strong>Settings &gt; Willpower System</strong>, which grey out when the system is disabled.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Reworked and expanded Autism Spectrum</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Replaced the old short fixation model with longer focused interests that last a few weeks and help regulation rather than directly boosting a skill.</li>
		<li>Stress and Load now build from sudden task changes, prolonged demands, unclear social situations, loud or crowded places, and sensory discomfort.</li>
		<li>The first two hours of practice are protected from demand-related buildup.</li>
		<li>Quiet rooms inside busy places, such as school toilets and the library, remain useful low-load spaces.</li>
		<li>Overload now uses full meltdown or shutdown scenes based on Willpower, location, and nearby characters.</li>
		<li>Added overload responses such as stimming, leaving, using Harper's card, or masking at a later cost.</li>
		<li>Stimming is also available as a normal action, with reduced benefit when it must be hidden in public.</li>
		<li>Clear, repetitive work such as cleaning and gardening pays better, while loud venues are more demanding.</li>
		<li>Harper's assessment now covers childhood signs, conversation, routine, sensory issues, and lasting interests, and explicitly separates autism from ADHD.</li>
		<li>Kylar now recognises masking and distinguishes their autistic traits from their obsessive/<em>yandere</em> behaviour.</li>
		<li>The trait grants two extra general Character Talents and one sex-skill Talent. Existing saves are converted automatically.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added an NPC Chastity slider</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added a 0–3 setting beside Bodywriting.</li>
		<li>At 0, NPCs do not initiate forced chastity, key-taking, Whitney's chastity rule or dildo-belt upgrade, pound chastity, defeat chastity, or Winter's storeroom device.</li>
		<li>At 1–3, these events can occur with increasing frequency.</li>
		<li>Voluntary chastity and NPCs maintaining a device they already gave you are unaffected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added an NPC Makeup frequency setting</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added a setting controlling how often NPCs change the player's makeup during encounters.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a body-variety option</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>X-Change flips can now also change the player's demeanour when enabled.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added foraging baskets</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The forest shop now sells mushroom, fruit, and flower baskets.</li>
		<li>Carrying one raises forage-find chances to 30% while walking and 50% while searching.</li>
		<li>80% of finds favour the selected basket category.</li>
		<li>Baskets can store 5 items, like bags. But cannot be used as school bags.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Water Dragon anti-Choice recovery</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Once the nest is fully clean, <strong>Search the shore</strong> can find a sealed lab case containing one anti-Choice pill while the Choice effect is active.</li>
		<li>It can only be found if the player does not already have a reversal.</li>
		<li>The pill is stored in the medicine drawer and cannot be taken while pregnant.</li>
		<li>Older saves are supported.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Water Dragon nesting access</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The coastal path can now appear from both Mer Street and the meadow after the player has laid a Water Dragon egg.</li>
		<li>Existing History-grade unlocks still work.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added an under-skirt encounter</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added an under-skirt encounter to Sydney's library lifting event.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Avery reconciliation after a soft dismissal</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery can appear at the pub once per week after moving on.</li>
		<li>The player may apologise once per appearance.</li>
		<li>Avery rejects the first three apologies and accepts the fourth, arranging a Saturday 8 PM meeting.</li>
		<li>Reconciliation restores Avery as an active NPC, raises Love, lowers Rage, and can restore love-interest status if normal requirements are met.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Robin shared gardening</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>When Robin offers to water the garden, the player can arrange to do it together after school.</li>
		<li>Robin waits until 5 PM, then waters alone if the player does not arrive.</li>
		<li>The arrangement can be started or cancelled from Robin's room and is unavailable while Robin is too upset.</li>
		<li>Watering, planting, tilling, and harvesting now reduce Stress, with Plant Lover background giving more relief.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded blindness and Ivory Wraith events</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Blindfolds and sleeping masks now properly block vision when worn over the eyes.</li>
		<li>Blindness intensifies sexual sensation but makes sexual actions harder, with a smaller penalty when self-imposed and reductions from higher skill.</li>
		<li>Several scenes now change when the player cannot see, including bed encounters and Ivory Wraith disguises.</li>
		<li>Gwylan can discuss the Wraith's mark after the tattoo conversation, and the mark can be confessed at the temple.</li>
		<li>Some creatures recognise the mark as another creature's claim and may avoid the player.</li>
		<li>An attached Wraith can intervene during extreme Blood Moon captivity or some heavily dissociated/entranced combats, except on the island or pirate ship.</li>
		<li>River and Sydney now offer more responses to sunglasses at school, including removing them, claiming light sensitivity, or attempting a skulduggery-based lie.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Poppy post-bad-end follow-up</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>If a bad end keeps the player away for more than three days, a one-use explanation option appears at Poppy's flat or the lake for the next two weeks. Resto their Patience.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Magpie's Luck</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Moor jewellery found while looting camps with Great Hawk is now much rarer at 1%.</li>
		<li>Found jewellery can now be worn or taken home instead of being scrapped for cloth.</li>
		<li>Finding jewellery unlocks <strong>Magpie's Luck</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated cooking and food values</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Increased the market value of seventeen dishes that previously sold for less than their ingredients, including macaroni cheese, cauliflower cheese, hamburgers, cheeseburgers, lasagne, carbonara, steak, and roast dinner.</li>
		<li>Reduced Belgian bun from £10 to £2 and Yorkshire pudding from £12 to £3.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated pregnancy acceptance</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Completed births now gradually raise the minimum Pregnancy Acceptance value, reaching full acceptance after five births.</li>
		<li>Acceptance slowly rises toward this minimum, faster while pregnant.</li>
		<li>The first pregnancy still receives no automatic acceptance increase, and prayer remains the fastest way to raise it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Buffed Charlie's classes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Completing Dancing, Yoga, or Heel classes now increases both Dancing and Willpower.</li>
		<li>Subscribers gain +2 Dancing and +2 Willpower per completed class.</li>
		<li>Dance Practice keeps its existing skill gains, with subscribers gaining an additional +2 Dancing and +2 Willpower.</li>
		<li>Non-subscribers now gain +1 Willpower from Dance Practice.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Made White so Pale a full trait</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>White so Pale</strong> is now a real trait/buff and reduces Physique decay by 20%.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated NPC pilling</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>X-Changed NPC penis sizes now reroll with each new pill.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Avery pilling</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery now distinguishes body sex from visible gender presentation.</li>
		<li>If a pill would make the player more like Avery, Avery instead asks for clothing or makeup changes where appropriate.</li>
		<li>Already X-Changed players are directed to adjust presentation instead of receiving another redundant pill.</li>
		<li>Previous identity disclosure is acknowledged.</li>
		<li>Invitations, mansion introductions, forced-pill routes, and stay-pilled reminders now use consistent logic.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Remy's farm pills</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Remy no longer applies a redundant Purple effect when it is already active.</li>
		<li>Breast growth stays within valid sizes and affected saves are repaired.</li>
		<li>The Herm effect now appears in the X-Change Traits list.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Water Dragon egg sales</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Harper haggling now correctly raises the egg price round by round, with the final debate requiring SSS English.</li>
		<li>Price increases already earned are kept even if a later round is lost.</li>
		<li>Fallen, Angel, and Demon income bonuses now apply to egg sales.</li>
		<li>Project Pelagos no longer treats a late summons as a refusal, and orderlies take the player to the correct scheduled room.</li>
		<li>Pregnancies ending in the lab only become Water Dragon egg pregnancies for a full Water Dragon.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Water Dragon and pirate journeys</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Demons can now masturbate during the Water Dragon crossing and in the pirate-ship bunk.</li>
		<li>If the current body cannot climax through masturbation, demonic burn can force a release when required.</li>
		<li>This exception only applies to those two journeys and only when purity must be burned.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated washing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bath and other washing boosts no longer count down while sleeping.</li>
		<li>The bath boost lasts slightly longer.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated public exposure and substance balance</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Smoking now requires repeated use before becoming addictive.</li>
		<li>Alcohol tolerance develops more gradually.</li>
		<li>Penetration Pain builds slightly slower, maximum Pain gives treatment advice, and sensitivity tooltips use cleaner values.</li>
		<li>Public exposure now increases Allure and Danger more consistently.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Gwylan clothing requests</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The first two requests still require shopping.</li>
		<li>Later requests have a 70% chance to ask for a suitable item already owned in its current colours.</li>
		<li>Favourites, school uniforms, and irreplaceable clothing are excluded.</li>
		<li>Wardrobe requests use the generic completion scene; special outfit scenes remain shopping-only.</li>
		<li>If the requested item is dyed or sold, its requested colour must be restored or the item bought again.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated chastity vow feedback</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Temporary X-Change bodies now correctly receive forgiveness.</li>
		<li>Permanent and original-body penetration still breaks the vow.</li>
		<li>Fixed missed Avery, portal, toy, and small-penis penetration paths.</li>
		<li>Traits, statistics, and legacy vow states remain synchronised.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Gate handhold virginity</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wearing gloves now gives the correct hand-virginity warning.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Water Dragon and Kylar narration</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Tidied Water Dragon narration and the Kylar prison escape text.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Bailey interactions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Kylar's owl now reacts to Bailey flirting, lap time, and Stress relief.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated tentacle targeting</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Tentacle targets now display readable labels in every combat-control mode, including Bath Slime and Gwylan encounters.</li>
		<li>Restored missing vaginal and chest tentacle actions.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated scaled sprite rendering</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Miniature, mini, and small character sprites now remain crisp instead of blurred.</li>
		<li>Sidebar body-size scaling is disabled by default.</li>
		<li>Rescaled <strong>Scale sidebar image to body size</strong> to reduce face deformation in GooseFem.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Reduced X-Change save-load lag</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Streamlined migration work performed when loading saves.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC hand tracking</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>NPC hand positions now stay synchronised during touching, fingering, withdrawal, and butt-plug removal, preventing stale-position errors such as those in Gwylan's forest scene.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed adult shop opening behaviour</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Corrected the adult shop grand opening hours and after-hours behaviour.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan's cream scene</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Giving up now has its own ending and no longer applies the damage penalty twice.</li>
		<li>Ending normally without Gwylan finishing no longer causes unnecessary Stress or Pain.</li>
		<li>The scene now closes correctly, preventing broken <strong>Next</strong> links, pronoun errors, and reopening a finished encounter.</li>
		<li>Affected saves recover automatically.</li>
		<li>Following Gwylan into the dark room now correctly describes following them rather than trying to escape.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed consensual encounter endings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Ending consensual sex no longer applies the normal end-of-fight damage, Stress, or Pain and no longer counts as giving up.</li>
		<li>Only <strong>Give Up</strong> during a hostile encounter counts as surrender.</li>
		<li>Scripted endings and reverse rape do not count as giving up.</li>
		<li>The player can give up three times per day and end consensual encounters five times per day; the button shows remaining uses and greys out at zero.</li>
		<li>Childbirth endings remain unlimited.</li>
		<li>Non-consensual encounters and consensual encounters that become hostile still use normal defeat consequences.</li>
		<li>Damage from actual attacks is unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery's private bar</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Corrected a pronoun typo.</li>
		<li>Avery's Rage now increases only when Avery actually notices the drink.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed purchases using the wrong affordability check</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Shops now check the same price shown on the purchase button and grey out unaffordable options.</li>
		<li>Fixed clothing and jewellery shops, spa, tailor, wardrobe repairs, sunscreen, several debt/payoff events, Bailey's cat ears, and photography.</li>
		<li>Card-game entry costs now match the amount added to the pot.</li>
		<li>Added a safety check preventing purchases from taking more cash than the player currently has.</li>
		<li>Shopping still uses wallet money only; savings must still be withdrawn first.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Disable semen volume loss</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The setting now prevents semen loss from all dry orgasms, including <strong>Cum like a girl</strong> and orgasms with no semen remaining, rather than only Micro or Mini penis cases.</li>
		<li>Updated the tooltip and exported settings text.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed high-HP feats and brawling rewards</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Enemy HP is now reset after every fight so high-HP feats use the enemy actually defeated rather than stale HP from a previous encounter.</li>
		<li>Brawling experience is now based on damage dealt in the current fight.</li>
		<li>Health added during a fight is counted correctly.</li>
		<li>Previously unlocked feats are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed encounter triggers and scene logic</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Restored several missing Avery Valentine's interactions, including mansion response, hand-holding on the drive home, cleaning-duty cat-fur dialogue, and lap dialogue.</li>
		<li>Fixed Gwylan's ritual so the resist-orgasm option appears correctly and Arousal increases in every position.</li>
		<li>Snow beasts now shred the outer clothing layer actually being worn.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed random NPCs inheriting named NPC data</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Strangers no longer inherit a previous named character's name, identity, stored data, or special protections.</li>
		<li>Generic NPCs use descriptions such as “the petite woman” until they genuinely introduce themselves.</li>
		<li>Characters the player has actually met still use their names.</li>
		<li>Fixed duplicate named-character entries that could make narration switch incorrectly to “they”.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragon egg-laying interruptions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Egg laying pauses while the player is trapped or inhabiting someone else's life, including in soft bad end, flashbacks, Hopeless Cycle.</li>
		<li>Countdown and labour resume once the player is free.</li>
		<li>Harper's lab remains separate and unaffected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed antiques becoming unsellable</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wearing the moor gold ring no longer deducts twice its value and pushes antique value negative.</li>
		<li>Affected saves are automatically refunded when loaded, restoring Winter and Journal antique-sale recognition.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed clothes failing to return after sleep</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Water Dragon egg events no longer leave the previous night's clothes stuck in storage.</li>
		<li>Returning to the bedroom recovers clothes still left beside the bed.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon wake-up events return stored clothing to the wardrobe before leaving.</li>
		<li>Repeated sleeping no longer strands older stored outfits.</li>
		<li>Robin's room now restores the player's saved hairstyle properly.</li>
		<li>Bedroom Blackmail Notice no longer skips normal clothing restoration.</li>
		<li>The fix also covers sleeping at the farm, temple, pirate ship, and other non-bedroom locations.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed plant tentacle nectar samples</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Roots, vines, and shoots can give nectar again.</li>
		<li>Sample counts now only show what Gwylan still needs and stop announcing extras once the request is complete.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Blood Moon pet boss behaviour</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Pets hatched or replaced during a Blood Moon are safe until the next Blood Moon.</li>
		<li>Reviving a pet killed by the boss no longer causes an immediate repeat kill or wastes the Elixir.</li>
		<li>Feeding, cleaning, and training remain available while the boss is stalking the pet.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed penetration Pain updating too often</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Penis-penetration Pain was previously added every time the character sprite refreshed.</li>
		<li>It is now checked once per combat turn and only during combat.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed orgasm denial and anal penetration checks</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Orgasm denial now checks what is actually penetrating the player rather than stale or empty action variables.</li>
		<li>Denial messages now name the correct missing craving, such as knot or pussy, instead of defaulting to dick.</li>
		<li>Anal penetration now applies the intended Pain and penis-addiction sensitivity effects.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gender Identity drift</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Disabling <strong>Update Gender Identity from your Identity system</strong> now stops daily Gender Identity drift as intended while still allowing event-driven changes.</li>
		<li>Statistics now correctly show when drift and body changes are disabled.</li>
		<li>Fixed notices firing at the wrong level, corrupted saves breaking the meter, sex-based daily drift bypassing the setting, and unexplained Stress at the Identity limit.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed makeup gender readings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Applying or removing makeup now updates gender appearance immediately, including blusher and custom cosmetics.</li>
		<li>School toilets and changing rooms now handle androgynous players consistently and use clearer wording when others force a binary judgement.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin's crossdressing scenes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Crossdressing dialogue now uses Robin's original sex where appropriate after an X-Change pill.</li>
		<li>Robin correctly remembers the Halloween costume worn, starts the correct trick-or-treating story, and wears the correct school uniform in the canteen.</li>
		<li>Dialogue now recognises that the pill physically changed Robin's body rather than treating it as only clothing.</li>
		<li>Updated orphanage door, visitor, Robin reaction, and infirmary scenes.</li>
		<li>Pilled Robin no longer uses padded bras or chest binders.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin's self-sufficiency</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Robin and other characters now recognise when Robin pays their own way.</li>
		<li>Robin can become independent when rent is collected at Poppy's flat.</li>
		<li>Automatic payments no longer skip the independence scene.</li>
		<li>Bailey no longer targets or uses an independent Robin as leverage.</li>
		<li>The player's rent remains at the normal rate once Robin pays their share.</li>
		<li>Invalid stand upgrades are rejected and existing save progress is handled more safely.</li>
		<li>Corrected Robin's payment, the player's remaining rent, and stand-income descriptions while removing redundant debt tracking.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Harper, staff, and islander pronoun perspective</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Harper, their staff, and islanders now use pronouns based on how they perceive the player's current body rather than the player's identity pronouns.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragon Lab</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Corrected combat initialisation.</li>
		<li>Prevented duplicate encounter cleanup.</li>
		<li>Serum retention now respects content settings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed farm watchtower issues</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Seducing the guard counts as the day's interaction even if the player backs out.</li>
		<li>Sparring and seduction reset correctly each day, including older saves.</li>
		<li>The current guard wage displays correctly.</li>
		<li>Seduction rejection now lowers Trust correctly and stops the guard following the player.</li>
		<li>Bank standing orders no longer erase a pay rise when wages are later paid in person.</li>
		<li>Paying collected wages no longer moves the player to the fields.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed balloon stall dialogue and seduction</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The stall owner keeps the correct pronouns and body throughout Robin's partnership and seduction scenes.</li>
		<li>Free drinks work in every season.</li>
		<li>Angry stall owners can reconcile over any drink.</li>
		<li>Cleaned up related dialogue and shop errors.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed skulduggery bonuses</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Transformation and clothing bonuses now help skulduggery checks without falsely making the underlying skill count as maxed.</li>
		<li>Reaching the actual skill cap now gives the correct learning feedback.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed urchin sidebar graphics</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Urchin graphics in the clitoris now display correctly in the sidebar image.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change state during Sydney encounters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>NPC body pills no longer break active sex positions.</li>
		<li>Sydney's prayer room preserves virginity history for each body.</li>
		<li>Added repair for affected saves and corrupted fluid statistics.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Hopeless Cycle cheats</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Hopeless Cycle cheat handling no longer breaks the cheat menu.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed redundant narration</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Removed the repeated “You get a good workout” line from the beach run.</li>
		<li>Fixed redundant fruit counting in Avery's mansion.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed minor Poppy Valentine issues</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Minor Poppy Valentine and Poppy bug fixes by Sei/Karl Sendis.</li>
		<li>Audited and bug-fixed by D.N.A.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Kylar autism dialogue</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Kylar now separates routines, counting, and bell-focused behaviour from the possessive actions they choose themselves.</li>
		<li>Their offer to keep others away while the player practises is no longer framed as part of the diagnosis.</li>
		<li>Fixed the park practice scene using &lt;&lt;his&gt;&gt; instead of “them”.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
